sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as CHIPS Participant<br/>(one of ~40)
    participant CH as CHIPS<br/>Queue and release engine
    participant FRB as Federal Reserve Bank of NY<br/>CHIPS account

    Note over P,FRB: MORNING: prefunding
    CH->>P: Opening position requirement<br/>set from recent activity
    P->>FRB: Fedwire transfer of opening position
    FRB-->>CH: Balance credited to participant position

    Note over P,CH: DAY: submission and continuous release
    loop Throughout the business day
        P->>CH: Submit payment orders
        CH->>CH: Balanced release algorithm:<br/>single, bilateral, multilateral offsets
        CH-->>P: Released payments are FINAL<br/>at the moment of release
    end

    alt Outbound queue is blocked
        P->>FRB: Supplemental funding via Fedwire
        FRB-->>CH: Position increased
        CH->>CH: Blocked payments release
    end

    Note over P,FRB: CLOSE: final netting and payout
    CH->>CH: Stop accepting new payments
    CH->>CH: Multilateral netting of everything<br/>still in the queue
    CH->>P: Notify closing position

    alt Participant owes a net amount
        P->>FRB: Fund the closing obligation via Fedwire
        FRB-->>CH: Received
    end

    CH->>CH: Release remaining queued payments
    CH->>FRB: Instruct payout of residual balances
    FRB->>P: Return residual balance via Fedwire

    Note over P,FRB: Every participant ends the day at zero.<br/>CHIPS carries no overnight credit exposure.
